{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"agent_message","text":"The sensitive routing reduction cannot be fused without changing its cancellation residue, so I reverted that experiment. A safer improvement combines the two independent shared-weight-gradient GEMMs into one larger GEMM and writes its packed input directly from the SwiGLU kernel; local profiling drops the large case from about 1.27 ms to 1.19 ms with unchanged numerical ratios. I’m testing whether independent GEMMs can also overlap safely on a secondary stream before the last verifier run."}}
